=== HINT 1 ===
Every recursive function needs:
  1. A base case that stops the recursion
  2. A recursive case that calls itself with a smaller input

=== HINT 2 ===
Base case: if n == 0 (or n <= 0), return 1
Recursive: return n * factorial(n - 1);

=== HINT 3 (SPOILER) ===
if (n <= 0) return 1;
return n * factorial(n - 1);
